#==============================================================================================
#
#   navigate_event - HTML::NavigateEvent, NavigationDestination, ErrorEvent and
#   extract_error_information
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       Port of Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/NavigateEvent.cpp (lines 1-297) without the JS-facing
#       intercept() and scroll() methods and their shared checks (phase 3: only a script's
#       intercept() moves an event's interception state off "none"), NavigationDestination.cpp
#       (lines 1-94, its JS getters excepted), ErrorEvent.cpp (lines 1-50) and
#       ErrorInformation.cpp (lines 14-70) for the values a page without script makes: a
#       DOMException, whose message is an accessor of its prototype (not an own property), so
#       the message is "Uncaught exception: " and the value as JS::Value's formatter writes an
#       object, and whose error data has no traceback before script runs.
#
#       Copyright (c) 2023, Andrew Kaster <akaster@serenityos.org>
#       Copyright (c) 2022, Andreas Kling <andreas@ladybird.org>
